WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.302
-Welcome back.
We're here with Ricky Gervais.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.171
I feel bad.
I didn't ask after your health.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.074
Have you managed to make it
through these last two years

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.242
without falling ill?

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.478
-Yeah. Well, yeah.
I mean, well --

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:16.315
I wouldn't say I'm healthy,
but I haven't caught COVID.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.652
I mean,
I'm 20 pounds overweight.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.421
I'm 60. I'm losing my hair.
I'm fat. I've got a bunion.

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:24.056
I've got bad knees.
I've got a bad back.

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:28.028
Back goes every now and again.
I'm a -- I'm a slob.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.563
I -- It's because
I eat and drink too much.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.699
I'm drunk now.
Because I'm in England.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.702
And I don't mean
because of the time zone.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.002
I mean it's compulsory.

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:38.304
If you're in England,
you've got to be drunk.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.573
It's one of the rules, right?

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.176
So -- But, yeah,
I haven't caught COVID, no.

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:46.746
Maybe I have.
I always wake up sort of sweaty

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.047
and anxious and feeling [bleep],

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.315
so I might have COVID.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.985
I don't know. But --
[ Laughs ] I wouldn't know.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.487
I wouldn't --

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.156
In fact, all the way through
the first year,

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.225
every time I woke up,
I thought I had COVID.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.227
But then I'd wake up,
if I've got a sore throat,

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.062
I'd go, "Jane, it's cancer."

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.763
And she goes, "No, it's not.
Go to the doctor."

00:01:04.763 --> 00:01:06.399
And I'd go, "Don't say that."
So I google it.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.301
And then the first five,
they go, "Oh, it's nothing."

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.702
And then I google too much,

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.704
and it goes -- this one's rare
and it's terminal.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.706
And I go, "I've got that one."

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.775
But apart from that, I'm --
Yeah, I'm well.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.110
-Yeah, good.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.946
-I'm in really good shape.
Mentally.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.315
-Do you think maybe all
the sort of awards behind you

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.718
created, like,
a natural immunity to it?

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.119
-Maybe.

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:29.789
It plays havoc with the Wi-Fi.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.225
Yeah, I'm in
Meryl Streep's house.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.760
Um, yeah.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.028
I didn't place them there.
They're there all the time.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.832
This is in my study.
It's not like I put them out.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.899
I'm on set when I put out all --

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:44.337
"Jane, get all the awards,
put them all behind me!"

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.773
-While we're talking
about awards, you sort of --

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.041
the Hollywood Foreign Press.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.575
The Golden Globes happened
a couple of weeks ago

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.977
just online.
It was a Twitter feed.

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:55.215
This is how far
the Golden Globes have fallen.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.750
I hosted it once. You hosted it
five times, very famously.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.419
I think you are the person
most associated with that.

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:03.289
Are you surprised
at where this has sort of led?

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.924
-Basically you're blaming me.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.726
You're trying to blame me,
aren't you?

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.128
-I only did it once, and
you did it, like, five times.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.796
-"I did it once.
And it was fine. It kept going.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.766
He did it five times.
It's done."

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.769
Well, I wouldn't
watch it anyway.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.106
The only time I've ever watched
an awards show, I'm at.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:23.909
I'm either winning or losing
an award or presenting it.

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:25.478
I loved it, though.
I thought it was great.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.915
I did it five times
over ten years.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.917
And it's funny because
the first time I did it,

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:37.656
I could feel particularly the
sort of Hollywood press, right?

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:40.025
They were going, "Who is this?
Who this is fat annoying Brit?"

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:42.995
How dare he --
How dare he make fun

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:47.467
of the most important people
in the world," right?

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.303
Over ten years, I kept going.
I kept doing the same thing.

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:52.939
But the world changed.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:56.042
And by the last one,
the public were going,

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.943
"Yeah, give it to 'em.
We're sick of celebrities.

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.045
We hate them.

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:02.849
We're tired of being lectured,
telling us to recycle

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.717
when they're going
on a private jet."

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:08.087
So I think ordinary people
were suddenly just --

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.790
They sort of turned
a little bit.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.293
They didn't --
They were sick of being told

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:17.096
what to do by rich people.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:22.035
So I think I hit a lucky streak
on the last one.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.737
But it was fun. It was just fun.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.806
It's not what I do,
but it was fun.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.709
-You do -- You have started
doing stand-up again.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.144
You have a new special
coming out on Netflix.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:34.880
Was this a hour,
or however long it is,

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.416
that you'd been working on
before the pandemic?

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:40.185
-Yeah, I did --

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:42.688
I did lots of gigs
and then just --

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:46.091
It just stopped
in sort of like --

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:49.561
February. Was it 2020?

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:53.465
And, yeah, I had, like,
over half still to go.

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:55.768
And it was amazing.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:59.739
Because people kept their
tickets for like two years.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:03.176
Which -- And then
I managed to finish it

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:06.812
between sort of
June and Christmas.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.548
And it was amazing.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:10.917
Because the atmosphere
was electric.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.987
I was so happy
to be back to normal.

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:17.289
I really am appreciating
my audience

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:18.657
more now than I ever did.

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:20.493
I really -- It really hit me.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.828
Almost on an emotional level.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.096
Because you think, you know,

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.998
that they're paying
hard-earned cash and

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.635
they've got to find a babysitter
and a parking space.

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:33.172
And I better have
something to say.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.607
But I really, really love it.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:37.276
I can't wait to start again.
And I've recorded the special.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:41.648
But now Netflix got to
translate it into 160 languages.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:43.583
I didn't know
there were 160 languages,

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.918
but apparently there are,
and that will be out in spring.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.320
But I'll be on a new one.
I can't wait to get back.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.090
I think it's my favorite thing
I do now, stand-up.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.226
-Do you worry about that lead
time after you record a special

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:58.197
and before it comes out
that any of the jokes will age?

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.866
-Yeah. Lots of things,
I think, you know --

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:06.204
Luckily, my set list is like,
you know, AIDS, famine, Hitler.

00:05:06.204 --> 00:05:07.874
And they're evergreen.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.441
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:12.845
They -- [ Laughs ]
They age really well.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.413
-So, like, the worst thing
that would happen to you

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:18.050
right now would be, like,
new Hitler news.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:21.154
-[ Laughs ] Yeah!
Exactly. Yeah.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:23.989
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:27.326
-If anything happened
where people are like,

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.294
"Oh, I'm going to
reconsider Hitler."

00:05:29.294 --> 00:05:30.630
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.799
Find out something.
"Oh, no. That ruins everything."

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:36.035
I do think that, though.
I do think that.

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.970
Like --

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.072
If Boris Johnson's not around.

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:42.274
I do one joke
about Boris Johnson,

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:46.946
and if he's not around, I go,
"Oh, no, that ruins that joke."

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.982
-I can't thank you enough
for being here, Ricky.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.852
I really do hope next time
you're in New York City with us.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.722
Ricky Gervais. All three
seasons of "After Life"

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:57.590
are currently streaming
on Netflix.

